content.text:
I'm confident enough to write up, with one caveat noted below. The travel-plan fault is the only one with a clear, user-facing chain. The traffic drops on other services look like a consequence of users giving up after failures rather than separate faults, and ts-cancel-service's disappearance rests on only 8 normal-period spans.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_response_body_corrupted",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "All travel-plan travelPlan server spans in the incident return HTTP 500 (841), with none in normal traffic."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND message LIKE '%JSON parse error%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Travel-plan logs 841 SEVERE errors: downstream response failed JSON parsing into Response<Integer>."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-seat-service' AND span_name LIKE '%left_tickets%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Seat-service left_tickets server spans all return 200 quickly (p95 about 17 ms), so the callee itself is healthy."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, round(sum(value),0) AS total FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='k8s.pod.network.errors' AND service_name IN ('ts-travel-plan-service','ts-seat-service') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Network error counters on travel-plan and seat pods are zero, so the fault is not a wire-level problem."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-travel-plan-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "ui-dashboard travelPlan requests return errors and take about 6-7 s at p50, versus about 0.6 s in normal traffic."}]}
  ]
}
```

